    "title": "Why NASA’s Artemis II Astronauts Won’t Land on the Moon - The New York Times",
    "text": "AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENT See more of our coverage in your search results.Encuentra más de nuestra cobertura en los resultados de búsqueda. Add The New York Times on GoogleAgrega The New York Times en Google NASA landed astronauts on the moon for the first time in 1969, and then five times more. So why is it that in 2026 NASA is talking about going back to the moon, but not landing on it?Landing people on the moon is difficult, and no one has done it since 1972.That’s because after Neil Armstrong stepped on the moon during Apollo 11, many Americans felt that the space race with the Soviet Union was won and that further lunar exploration was not worth the expense. In the decades since, NASA has focused on low-Earth orbit with the space shuttles and the International Space Station.Subscribe to The Times to read as many articles as you like.Kenneth Chang, a science reporter at The Times, covers NASA and the solar system, and research closer to Earth.Share full articleRelated ContentAdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTSupport independent journalism with a subscription. Already a subscriber? Log in.Enjoy unlimited access for $1 a week.Welcome offer$7.50 $1/weekBilled as $4 every four weeks for your first six months, then $30 thereafter. Continue with cardPayPalCancel or pause anytime.All Access includes news, plus Games, Cooking, Audio, Wirecutter and The Athletic.Offer for a New York Times All Access subscription. Current subscribers and those who have previously accepted a sale/introductory offer from The New York Times may be ineligible for another sale/introductory offer. Subscription excludes print edition. Some games may be available without a subscription. You will be automatically charged in advance $4.00 every 4 weeks for 6 months, and $30.00 every 4 weeks thereafter. Cancel before October 29, 2026 to avoid the transition to the standard price that will be charged on that date. You can cancel prior to renewal from your account settings online or du